      "id": 163081,
      "name": "morph147",
      "username": "morph147",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/839c29/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-21T21:26:10.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Phantom5613\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/48/1906_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Phantom5613:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Any idea what it was in the update that did this?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>speculating based off what I do for a living but when it opens that window the program should say put it here based off some kind of pixel coordinates. With the reduction project they did and the update to the unreal system either A) it has to do with compressing files and their coordinates are now off or B) the unreal engine changed what they call the origin and their centering pixel values needs to be modified.</p>",
